    summary: "AI-assisted automation extends Chapter 11's principle of automating mechanics while reserving judgment for a human review step. Starting narrow, confirming the underlying process works before automating it, and keeping a regular review step in place is what turns automation into something genuinely trustworthy \u2014 as it became for the bookkeeper who finally took a real week off.",
    takeaways: ["Automate mechanics; keep judgment calls with a human.", "Automating a broken process just breaks it faster, at scale.", "Start narrow and specific; expand only after proven reliability."]
